# The digest of each version of the Reply plugin package, plugins/reply: one line per version, the version, a space, and
# the sha256 of the whole package as the runtime computes it — the number `jason plugin list` shows for an installed copy.
# It is the digest of the package a release publishes, which that release's runtime reports in `system.info`'s
# `released_plugins`; it is not the archive's checksum in `checksums.txt`. From 0.20.0 on, each release's manifest carries
# the whole list as plugins.reply.recorded, from which `jason update check` reads an installed copy's version by digest.
# The list starts with 0.3.2, the package of the first release that published it as an asset (v0.11.0), and holds the
# versions a release published after it. From 0.9.0 on it holds every version the package has had, published or not,
# because every bump appends a line.
# A version is its content: any change to a file of the package is a new version, and a new version appends its line at
# the end, after the last edit to the package, since every edit changes the digest; once the version is bumped, the
# package's test prints the line to append. A line already here is never changed, and a line that changes or disappears
# in a diff is refused in review.
